-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- replay (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §7.3 “Consequences”)
-- a run is reproduced from the world's responses: a recording world keeps, beside its own state,
-- the responses given (encoded as words by the signature's encoder), and a replaying world answers
-- from such a record alone. The run under the replaying world has the same outcome: replay is a
-- property of the process and the responses, not of the world's internals
Encoder : Sig → Type
Encoder S = (c : Cmd S) → Resp S c → Word
